<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banda Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banda Islands are a small group of islands in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> that were the world's only source of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nutmeg">nutmeg</a> and mace in the early modern period. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> conquered them in 1621, killing or expelling most of the inhabitants. The islands were then worked as plantations by enslaved labourers under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banda-islands.jpg" alt="Banda Islands" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo by Mark Richards · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BandaBesarIslandSeenFromFortBelgica.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
